                            "slur"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b982ab36-e917-4cb2-9c28-7ad8f5a69b21",
                                "sense_id": "d3962ab4-cc68-3ddd-80a0-b0d09792d81c",
                                "text": "The windmill under the care of Mr. Kinney, a kind hearted old Englishman, was to me a source of infinite interest and pleasure. The old man always seemed pleased when he saw a troop of darkey little urchins, with their tow-linen shirts fluttering in the breeze, approaching to view and admire the whirling wings of his wondrous machine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "259b2820-afd1-4c38-8fcd-579ca8cbebaf",
                                "sense_id": "d3962ab4-cc68-3ddd-80a0-b0d09792d81c",
                                "text": "Sometimes we overhear others saying, \"Them colored people were slaves\" down in Tennessee. The children feel hurt when they hear such remarks; but I tell them it was no disgrace in Tennessee to belong to Colonel Anderson. Many darkeys would have been proud, as I used to be, to call you master."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
